meta {
  name: 1 Device Lifecycle
}

docs {
  # Scenario 1 — Device Lifecycle (b/c)

  Run the requests in order, nothing to fill in: members are the deterministic demo
  cast (m-1 Morgan Lee, m-2 Sam Carter — seeded by `../strata.core`'s demo profile),
  and request 1 generates a fresh device id per run so the scenario is repeatable.

  1. Register the device to Member m-1 — a new active mapping (201, nothing superseded)
  2. Send the identical registration again — idempotent: the same mapping id comes back
  3. Register the same device to m-2 — supersede: m-1's mapping is ended (kept for
     audit), the response names the superseded member
  4. No API key — rejected, nothing created

  Verify the audit trail (optional):
  psql: SELECT user_id, external_id, ended_at FROM user_external_ids
        WHERE external_id LIKE 'SM-SCN1-%' ORDER BY registered_at;
  — m-1's row survives with ended_at set; m-2's row is the active one (ended_at NULL).
}
